{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed two storey side and rear extensions by reason of the \r\nrearward siting in close proximity to the shared boundary with no 40 \r\nSequoia Park and the change in levels between the two sites, with no 40 \r\nSequoia Park being on a lower level, would result in an overbearing and \r\nobtrusive form of development, which would have an unacceptable \r\nimpact on the neighbouring amenities of the occupiers at no  40 Sequoia \r\nPark with regard to loss of outlook. In addition, the added height and \r\nmassing of the roof in conjunction with the site levels would have an \r\nunacceptable impact upon the appearance of the host dwelling and the \r\nimmediate streetscene resulting in an incongruous development that \r\nwould appear at odds with the scale and heights of houses on either side. \r\nOverall, the proposed development is contrary to the National Planning \r\nPolicy Framework (2024), Policy D3, D(7) of The London Plan (2021), \r\npolicy GR1 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041) and the adopted \r\nSupplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
